WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.468 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Our next guest
is an Oscar-nominated

00:00:01.468 --> 00:00:04.037 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Golden Globe and
Emmy Award-winning actress

00:00:04.037 --> 00:00:05.271 line:92%
you know from over 50 films,

00:00:05.271 --> 00:00:07.640 size:84% position:42%
including such classics
as "Bye Bye Birdie,"

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:09.876 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Carnal Knowledge,"
and "Viva Las Vegas."

00:00:09.876 --> 00:00:11.611 line:92%
She stars in "Queen Bees,"

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:13.880 size:75% position:38%
which is in theaters
and on demand now.

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:15.815 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Let's take a look.

00:00:17.317 --> 00:00:20.820
-Are you flirting with that gu
with the squirrel on his head?

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:24.724 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Esther said
he's a wonderful lover.

00:00:24.724 --> 00:00:26.092 line:92%
-Oh, and here comes my lunch

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:28.028 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I bet he takes Viagra.
-Mm.

00:00:28.028 --> 00:00:30.864 align:start size:94% position:6%
-From the looks on the faces
of the ladies,

00:00:30.864 --> 00:00:35.101
he's buying it by the truckload.
[ Laughs ]

00:00:45.745 --> 00:00:48.415 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Please welcome to the sho
Ann-Margret!

00:00:48.415 --> 00:00:51.317 align:start size:94% position:6%
Ann-Margret, I am thrilled
you are here.

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:53.286 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughing ]

00:00:53.286 --> 00:00:56.656 line:92%
I'm just laughing at that scene.

00:00:56.656 --> 00:00:57.824 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Ah. How you doing?

00:00:57.824 --> 00:00:59.793 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm doing well.
-Nice to meet you.

00:00:59.793 --> 00:01:01.661 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It is so nice to meet you
as well.

00:01:01.661 --> 00:01:04.497 align:start size:94% position:6%
We have very little in common,
but we do have one thing,

00:01:04.497 --> 00:01:07.901 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is we both went
to Northwestern University

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:11.137 size:84% position:42%
But you had a very --
a very short time there

00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:16.609 align:start size:94% position:6%
because you were discovered...
in your first year there?

00:01:16.609 --> 00:01:17.944 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, let's see.

00:01:17.944 --> 00:01:20.380 line:92%
No. I went one whole year.

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:27.554
And then a group that I was with
from Northwestern

00:01:27.554 --> 00:01:29.289 line:92%
called the Suttletones --

00:01:29.289 --> 00:01:32.926 align:start size:94% position:6%
took us three hours
to get that name --

00:01:32.926 --> 00:01:34.627 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
at The Hut.

00:01:34.627 --> 00:01:36.129 line:92%
Is it still there, The Hut

00:01:36.129 --> 00:01:39.232 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don't think The Hut
is still there, no.

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:42.535 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ] Oh, no.

00:01:42.535 --> 00:01:44.471 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Oh, how embarrassing.

00:01:44.471 --> 00:01:46.706 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Okay.

00:01:46.706 --> 00:01:48.308 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Mr. Burns --

00:01:48.308 --> 00:01:49.742 size:78% position:39% line:92%
I auditioned for him.

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:52.412 align:start size:94% position:6%
And everything really starte
from there,

00:01:52.412 --> 00:01:55.915 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause he took me in his sho
in Las Vegas

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:59.419 size:75% position:38% line:92%
at the Sahara hotel.

00:01:59.419 --> 00:02:01.221 line:92%
Everything started from there.

00:02:01.221 --> 00:02:03.289 align:start size:94% position:6%
I loved it.
-And early in your career,

00:02:03.289 --> 00:02:07.760 align:start size:94% position:6%
you worked with people,
you know, like Elvis Presley

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:09.229 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Steve McQueen.

00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:11.364 align:start size:94% position:6%
Are your memories of those
still vivid?

00:02:11.364 --> 00:02:15.969 align:start size:94% position:6%
Does that feel like
a completely other time?

00:02:15.969 --> 00:02:17.837 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, no, no, no.
I remember that.

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:23.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
I remember everything workin
with those two gentlemen.

00:02:23.676 --> 00:02:26.679 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Also, with McQueen,

00:02:26.679 --> 00:02:28.748 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I love motorcycles,

00:02:28.748 --> 00:02:31.551 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, of course,
he loved motorcycles.

00:02:31.551 --> 00:02:36.523 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the studio was giving me
a lot of trouble

00:02:36.523 --> 00:02:41.027 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I was very young
and they were --

00:02:41.027 --> 00:02:44.597 line:92%
and I drove it to the studio

00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:50.203
and they got very nervous an
did not want me to drive it.

00:02:50.203 --> 00:02:53.306 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so McQueen just said,
"Oh, forget about it.

00:02:53.306 --> 00:02:53.940 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
That's their job.

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:56.009 align:start size:94% position:6%
They have to be nervous
about something."

00:02:56.009 --> 00:02:58.511 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I kept driving it.
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:58.511 --> 00:03:03.183
At what point in your life
did you stop riding motorcycles?

00:03:03.183 --> 00:03:04.250 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-I have not stopped.

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:07.754 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ] I'm very, very
happy to hear that.

00:03:07.754 --> 00:03:09.289 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, this is
a little embarrassing

00:03:09.289 --> 00:03:12.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
because now I'm very familia
with your career,

00:03:12.325 --> 00:03:15.195 align:start size:94% position:6%
but it dawned on me today
that the first time

00:03:15.195 --> 00:03:18.097 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think I heard your voice
was when you played

00:03:18.097 --> 00:03:21.901 align:start size:94% position:6%
the "Flintstones" characte
Ann-Margrock.

00:03:21.901 --> 00:03:24.103 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Do you remember that?

00:03:24.103 --> 00:03:27.807 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, with Pebbles.
-[ Laughs ] It was...

00:03:27.807 --> 00:03:30.276 align:start size:94% position:6%
You guys were wonderful
together.

00:03:30.276 --> 00:03:31.344 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:31.344 --> 00:03:33.880 line:92%
-Thank you. I'll tell her.

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:35.315 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-So, this show --

00:03:35.315 --> 00:03:36.549 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
sorry, this film --

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:39.018 align:start size:94% position:6%
has sort of been described
as "Mean Girls"

00:03:39.018 --> 00:03:42.088 align:start size:94% position:6%
in a retirement home,
but it's also very sweet.

00:03:42.088 --> 00:03:43.823 line:92%
We saw in the clip we showed

00:03:43.823 --> 00:03:46.292 size:84% position:42%
the very funny people
you are working with --

00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:48.461 line:92%
Jane Curtin, Christopher Lloyd

00:03:48.461 --> 00:03:51.097
You also work with Ellen Burstyn
in this film.

00:03:51.097 --> 00:03:53.499 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is actually
your third film together.

00:03:53.499 --> 00:03:55.401 align:start size:94% position:6%
But is it true that
it's the first time

00:03:55.401 --> 00:03:57.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
you've ever done
a scene together?

00:03:57.937 --> 00:03:59.939 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-The very first time.

00:03:59.939 --> 00:04:02.842 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because I always...
In the other two films,

00:04:02.842 --> 00:04:05.044 line:92%
I played the other woman,

00:04:05.044 --> 00:04:08.781 align:start size:94% position:6%
so we didn't have
any scenes together.

00:04:08.781 --> 00:04:12.585
-There's something during th
pandemic that you've maintained,

00:04:12.585 --> 00:04:14.654 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is --
-[ Vocalizing ]

00:04:14.654 --> 00:04:15.255 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:15.255 --> 00:04:17.757 align:start size:94% position:6%
You've maintained a traditio
during the pandemic

00:04:17.757 --> 00:04:19.759 align:start size:94% position:6%
which I think is very nice
for people.

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:23.696
So many of us did not get to
have enough human interaction.

00:04:23.696 --> 00:04:28.635 align:start size:94% position:6%
You do a Friday dinner
with the same pair of friends.

00:04:28.635 --> 00:04:31.371 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes! Oh, yes.

00:04:31.371 --> 00:04:36.042 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's one of my former dancers,
Tommy Peel,

00:04:36.042 --> 00:04:39.846 line:92%
and his partner, Denny Dugan

00:04:39.846 --> 00:04:45.084 align:start size:94% position:6%
After my husband, Roger,
passed away --

00:04:45.084 --> 00:04:48.354 line:92%
it's now been four years -

00:04:48.354 --> 00:04:49.555 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Tommy said to me,

00:04:49.555 --> 00:04:53.426 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I want you to come over
for dinner every Friday night.

00:04:53.426 --> 00:04:56.596 align:start size:94% position:6%
So it's been that way
for four years.

00:04:56.596 --> 00:04:58.865 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, see, I don't cook,
and I don't care.

00:04:58.865 --> 00:05:01.934 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughing ]
So the only way I can --

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:04.771 line:92%
No. It's been so wonderful

00:05:04.771 --> 00:05:05.972 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's great.

00:05:05.972 --> 00:05:08.775 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Are there any parts
of your career,

00:05:08.775 --> 00:05:09.475 line:92%
anything you look back --

00:05:09.475 --> 00:05:12.445 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause it's been such a storie
and accomplished career.

00:05:12.445 --> 00:05:15.782 align:start size:94% position:6%
Anything you wish you coul
go back and relive?

00:05:15.782 --> 00:05:23.723 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No. I want to just remember i
the way it was.

00:05:23.723 --> 00:05:26.626 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause, like,
with movies and everything

00:05:26.626 --> 00:05:32.031
I did the very best I coul
in whatever movie it was

00:05:32.031 --> 00:05:34.033 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I don't want
to revisit that.

00:05:34.033 --> 00:05:38.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
-'Cause it's true, you don't g
back and watch your work.

00:05:38.171 --> 00:05:39.205 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Is that correct?

00:05:39.205 --> 00:05:42.141 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, I can't sit
and gaze at myself.

00:05:42.141 --> 00:05:43.409 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughing ] No.

00:05:43.409 --> 00:05:45.011 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
No, no, no, no. No.

00:05:45.011 --> 00:05:49.349 align:start size:94% position:6%
I put everything I have
into whatever film I'm doing

00:05:49.349 --> 00:05:50.750 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
So that's it.

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:54.387 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, we appreciate
that you do and that you did

00:05:54.387 --> 00:05:56.022 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I can tell you,
from where I'm sitting,

00:05:56.022 --> 00:05:59.058 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's very easy to gaze
at yourself,

00:05:59.058 --> 00:06:00.560 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I've enjoyed it
for a very long time.

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:03.996
And thank you for making tim
for us today, Ann-Margret.

00:06:03.996 --> 00:06:07.233 size:78% position:39%
-Oh, what a pleasure.
Thank you so much.

00:06:07.233 --> 00:06:10.603 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Queen Bees" is in theaters
and on demand now.

